Sval: the faster backend removes what a removed install target installed

FasterMakeBackend gives each install target under dist/bin its own
install manifest and .track file. A target that leaves the build has no
manifest, so its .track is never processed and its files stay in
dist/bin, which a reused objdir then runs and packages. After writing
the manifests, the backend processes every orphaned .track with an empty
manifest (python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/sval_stale_installs.py).

